            <ArticleTitle>Stent shortening and elongation: pitfalls with the Wiktor coronary endoprosthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>233-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report demonstrates two specific complications that occurred during implantation of a Wiktor (Medtronic, Inc., Minneapolis, MN) coronary stent: stent shortening and elongation were observed and attributed to the unique coil structure of the device. Major cardiac events occurred during follow-up as a consequence of this stent deformation. Therefore, semiurgent bypass surgery should be considered to treat this complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
